## Manifest `.kyora/manifest.json`
```
{"entry": "index.html", "engine": "$engine", "scripts": ["<every classic script you load, relative path>"], "modules": ["<every ES module you load>"], "tests": ["tests/browser-tests.js"], "version": 1}
```
Every listed file must exist. Kyora checks the syntax of every listed script.

## Tests
- `tests/browser-tests.js` runs inside the preview page through the Kyora harness. Register exactly one test per browser acceptance id listed in KYORA_TESTSPEC.md, with that id written literally, for example `KyoraTest.test('at-01', 'name', async (t) => { ... })` (no alias or computed ids: Kyora scans for `KyoraTest.test('<id>'`).
- Optional `tests/logic-tests.mjs` (node:test) for acceptance tests of kind `node`; name each test starting with its id.
- Never delete or weaken tests. If a test is wrong, fix the test so it checks the behaviour the plan describes.

## Controls
- Keyboard and touch for every action. Touch targets at least 44x44 px. The HUD must stay readable on a 390x760 phone screen.
